  "body": "Stacked on #2997. GitHub cannot base a PR on a fork branch, so the diff below also shows the commits of #2997 (branch `mkinney:issue/2987-table-tilted-first-traverse`, merged here at 05c9e56f2). Merge #2997 first. Then this PR takes `git merge origin/main` and only its own commits stay.\n\n## What changed\n\nAfter a tool change the post sends Z, then X/Y at that height, then the block with the rotary words (`fanuc.cps` `xyFirst`, `traverseZ`, `onRapid`). The Z of that traverse is the higher of the clearance height and the start. The #2901 law did not judge the rotary, multi-axis and cross-drill kinds. Now each kind has a law or a named refusal:\n\n- **Rotary kinds** (Rotary Contour, Rotary Parallel, Rotary Offset): the new law `sim::verify::first_traverse_low_swept`.\n  - The rotary words come after the X/Y traverse, so the law reads the work swept through a full turn about the fitted axis. It reads the stock and part points, and the steel that turns with the work (a chuck), at its corners.\n  - It reads the fixed steel (table, tailstock) at its machine-frame top.\n  - It reads the start at its machine height over the axis line, lifted to the clearance height.\n  - The mounted machine selects the law. A machine whose work tilts gets the swept law. A machine whose head tilts gets the tip law. An unstated or mixed machine gets both laws.\n  - When no axis can be fitted, generation is refused by name.\n- **Multi-axis kinds** (5-Axis Contour, 5-Axis Parallel, Swarf, Advanced Swarf, Multi-Axis Rough, 5-Axis Flow, Multi-Axis Contour): the #2901 law on the tip in the part frame, at the post's traverse height.\n- **Cross drill on a mill**: generation refuses it by name before any move (\"cross holes are live-tooling work\"). A test pins this refusal.\n- **Cross drill on a lathe or a mill-turn**: this law does not judge it. The decision file records the limit. Refs #3077, which owns the gap.\n- **Verdict**: the same blocking `Warning::FirstTraverseLow`. The post gate, the UI, MCP and the warned moves do not change.\n- **Cache**: the op stamp of these kinds gets one more word (`first-traverse-2965`). Such a cache reads Stale once. The salt stays at v4, so no other stamp moves.\n\nDropped options: a reading at the start angle only (the rotary words come after the traverse); a sweep for the multi-axis kinds (no axis line is stated for them); a blanket refusal; a new `Warning` variant; a salt bump to v5 for all kinds. The decision file has the reasons: `docs/decisions/2965-first-traverse-rotary.md`.\n\n## Examples (stamp-only regeneration, accepted by the maintainer)\n\n- `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj` (Journal) and `examples/guide-multiaxis.camproj` (Swarf1) were regenerated. Only the operation `stamp` field of each file changes (`git diff --word-diff`).\n- Every `.nc` file and every golden is byte-identical.\n- The `WRITE_GOLDEN` run also rewrote the last digit of 7 A words in `first-continuous-4axis-part.nc`. That change was discarded, and the suite passes with the committed program. #3063 owns that drift.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New, `crates/app/tests/first_traverse_rotary.rs`:\n  - `a_rotary_kind_reads_its_square_bar_swept_about_the_axis`\n  - `a_5_axis_kind_reads_a_far_clamp_over_its_clearance_plane`\n  - `a_cross_drill_on_a_mill_is_refused_before_any_traverse`\n- New `camcraft-sim` unit tests in `verify::first_traverse::tests`:\n  - `a_turned_bar_is_read_at_its_corner_radius_not_its_upright_top`\n  - `a_radial_start_reads_its_radius_over_the_axis_line`\n  - `a_chuck_turns_with_the_work_and_a_tailstock_stands_still`\n  - `the_swept_top_follows_the_axis_tilt_and_refuses_no_input`\n\n## Quick gate (on 49e5d66e7 and 10cfd0cd2, with -j 18, before the merge of 05c9e56f2)\n\n- `camcraft-sim` lib first_traverse: 8/8 pass.\n- `camcraft-app`:\n  - first_traverse_rotary 3/3, rotary_verify 9/9, setup_align_multiaxis 10/10.\n  - first_traverse 4/4, first_traverse_table 5/5, operations 120 pass (6 ignored).\n  - continuous_4axis_part 10/10.\n  - post_not_judged, rotary_fixtures, center_cut_multiaxis, coarse_laws, cross_drill_neighbours, drilling_cross_stock, drilling_cross_box, stale_rapid_law, deburr_cache_stamp, wire_stamp: all pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The merge of 05c9e56f2 (#2997's table fix) was clean. The stack gate of the coordinator covers this merged head.\n- Heavy lanes not run, covered by the cut gate.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A machine with two rotaries: the rotary kinds read the sweep about the one fitted axis only.\n- A multi-axis pose that leans the tool down from its tip.\n- The tool radius under the tip (the same as #2901).\n\nRefs #3077\n\nChangelog: The first traverse after a tool change is now judged for the rotary, multi-axis and cross-drill operations; a clearance height inside the swept stock or under a fixture holds the post by name.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #2965\n",
